### 8.1 WiFi Discovery & Monitoring

The purpose of this challenge is to develop practical skills in wireless network discovery and security assessment. It focuses on using tools from the Aircrack-ng to identify nearby wireless networks and analyze their security configurations.

The `Aircrack-ng` suite is a collection of open-source tools designed for wireless network auditing and security testing. It is widely used by cybersecurity professionals and ethical hackers to assess the security of Wi-Fi networks by capturing packets, analyzing encryption protocols, and testing the strength of wireless passwords.

The suite supports a range of functions including network discovery, packet capture, monitoring wireless traffic, and performing cryptographic analysis of captured data. It is commonly used in controlled environments to evaluate vulnerabilities in wireless configurations such as weak encryption (WEP/WPA/WPA2), misconfigured access points, and insecure authentication methods.

Aircrack-ng consists of several command-line utilities that cover the entire security testing workflow for wireless networks. Tools like airmon-ng manage interfaces in monitor mode, airodump-ng captures packets, and aireplay-ng injects or replays traffic. The main component, aircrack-ng, performs key-cracking on captured WPA/WPA2 handshakes using dictionary or brute-force attacks.

#### Aircrack-ng Suite Components

| Component       | Function                                                                 | Command Syntax |
|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|
| aircrack-ng    | Cracks WEP/WPA/WPA2 keys using captured handshake files                | `aircrack-ng <capture-file>.cap -w <wordlist.txt>` |
| airodump-ng    | Captures wireless traffic and displays nearby networks and clients     | `airodump-ng <interface>` |
| airmon-ng      | Enables monitor mode on wireless interfaces                             | `airmon-ng start <interface>` |
| aireplay-ng    | Performs packet injection and deauthentication attacks                  | `aireplay-ng --deauth <count> -a <BSSID> <interface>` |
| airbase-ng     | Creates rogue/fake access points for testing                            | `airbase-ng -e <ESSID> -c <channel> <interface>` |
| airolib-ng     | Builds and manages WPA/WPA2 password databases                          | `airolib-ng <database> --import passwd <wordlist.txt>` |
| packetforge-ng | Crafts custom wireless packets for injection                            | `packetforge-ng -0 -a <BSSID> -h <source-mac> -k <dest-ip> -l <source-ip>` |

